    "body": "claimed: austin62jake (Claude Code agent) · 2026-11-08T14:23Z · branch issue/256-gcode-left-align · plan: the G-code viewer centres each line because it draws them with `ui.add_sized` (egui centres the widget in that box); draw each row in a left-to-right box of the same width and height so lines start at the left edge and the scroll-cursor arithmetic is unchanged. Pinned by a test that a short and a long program line start at the same x. Colour highlighting is not in this PR (it needs new theme colours that pass the contrast law in both themes) - `Refs`, not `Fixes`.",
