    "body": "partial fix on issue/256-gcode-left-align · PR #297 (draft) · pinned by `every_gcode_line_starts_at_the_listings_left_edge` (+ `a_line_wider_than_the_viewer_stays_on_one_row`) · `Refs`, not `Fixes`\n\nThe left alignment is done: lines were centred because each was drawn with egui's `add_sized`. The same call also let a line wider than the window wrap onto a second row, which put the scroll cursor off by a row below it; that's fixed too.\n\n**Syntax colouring is left for a decision**, because it adds colours the theme law has to vet. A proposal, if wanted:\n- line numbers and comments `( )` in the theme's `text_dim`;\n- `G0` in the palette's rapid colour and `G1`/`G2`/`G3` in its feed colour, so the listing matches the viewport's path colours (`colorvision::Semantic::rapid` / `feed`, already colour-vision aware);\n- `T`, `S` and `M` words in the accent; everything else in body text.\n\nEach colour would need to pass `contrast::BODY` (4.5:1) against the viewer's window ground in both built-in themes and every colour-vision mode, and user theme files might need keys for them. The row geometry wouldn't change (a `LayoutJob` per row in place of the `RichText`).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
